{{!--
  GH-197: click-to-zoom fullscreen overlay for `image::`/Kroki diagram
  blocks marked `role=zoom-in` (image-zoom.css's own header explains the
  affordance half — cursor/hover for a mouse, a persistent badge for
  touch). This partial is the dialog half only; wired up by
  src/js/14-image-zoom.ts, which discovers every `.zoom-in` image/diagram
  on the page at load and populates `.image-zoom-dialog__content` with a
  clone of whichever one was activated.

  Included once from default.hbs/home.hbs/home-single.hbs (not header.hbs,
  unlike search-dialog.hbs — this dialog has no fixed trigger of its own to
  live near; it exists purely so SOMETHING on the page can open it), so it
  is present on every page shape a zoomable image or diagram could actually
  appear on.

  Same `<dialog>` + `.dt-overlay`/`.dt-modal` composition search-dialog.hbs
  already uses, and the same reason: `showModal()` alone gives the top
  layer, the platform focus trap, Esc-to-close and an implicit ::backdrop,
  which 14-image-zoom.ts only needs to add backdrop-click-to-close on top
  of (search-dialog.hbs's own header has the full stacking-order
  argument for why `.dt-overlay__content` and `.dt-modal` must be SIBLINGS,
  in that DOM order, both inside `.dt-overlay` — repeated exactly here, not
  re-derived).

  Unlike the search dialog, `.dt-modal--fullscreen` is authored here
  directly, statically, never toggled by JS — there is no small/medium
  panel size that makes sense for "look at this image bigger"; every
  breakpoint gets the fullscreen frame.

  `.image-zoom-dialog__content` ships empty: 14-image-zoom.ts clones
  whichever `img`/`svg`/`embed` (or, for a diagram, the whole
  `.docouture-diagram__content` card) was activated into it on open, and
  empties it again on close so a stale clone never flashes on the next
  open.
--}}
<dialog id="image-zoom-dialog" class="image-zoom-dialog" aria-label="Zoomed image">
  <div class="dt-overlay dt-overlay--visible image-zoom-dialog__overlay">
    <div class="dt-overlay__content"></div>
    <div class="dt-modal dt-modal--fullscreen image-zoom-dialog__panel">
      <div class="dt-modal__container image-zoom-dialog__container">
        <button type="button" class="dt-button dt-button--ghost dt-button--icon-only image-zoom-dialog__close" aria-label="Close zoomed image">
          <span class="dt-button__content">
            <span class="dt-button__icon dt-button__icon-icon">{{icon "x"}}</span>
          </span>
        </button>
        <div class="image-zoom-dialog__content"></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</dialog>
